WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.300
You've built a following.

2
00:00:01.811 --> 00:00:03.100
Ten thousand people.

3
00:00:03.541 --> 00:00:04.830
Maybe a hundred thousand.

4
00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:06.467
You post every day.

5
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:07.814
The likes roll in.

6
00:00:08.417 --> 00:00:10.971
But here's the hard truth — you don't own

7
00:00:11.029 --> 00:00:11.714
any of it.

8
00:00:12.666 --> 00:00:14.176
Today we're talking about the difference

9
00:00:14.199 --> 00:00:15.836
between being a creator and being a

10
00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:16.405
builder.

11
00:00:17.008 --> 00:00:19.063
And why one path gives you real power,

12
00:00:19.272 --> 00:00:20.944
while the other keeps you renting.

13
00:00:20.944 --> 00:00:22.209
Let's define terms.

14
00:00:22.453 --> 00:00:24.590
A creator makes content on platforms they

15
00:00:24.648 --> 00:00:25.530
don't control.

16
00:00:25.855 --> 00:00:26.644
Instagram.

17
00:00:26.888 --> 00:00:27.585
TikTok.

18
00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:28.525
YouTube.

19
00:00:28.966 --> 00:00:30.708
You're creating value, yes.

20
00:00:31.219 --> 00:00:32.925
But the platform owns the relationship

21
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.866
with your audience.

22
00:00:34.307 --> 00:00:36.281
They decide what gets shown.

23
00:00:36.606 --> 00:00:37.953
They change the algorithm.

24
00:00:38.278 --> 00:00:39.624
They can ban you tomorrow.

25
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.540
You're renting space in someone else's

26
00:00:41.598 --> 00:00:42.086
house.

27
00:00:42.689 --> 00:00:43.444
And the rent?

28
00:00:43.885 --> 00:00:46.765
It's your time, your energy, your ideas.

29
00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:48.019
Now meet the builder.

30
00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.318
A builder creates things they own.

31
00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:51.502
A website.

32
00:00:51.827 --> 00:00:52.535
An app.

33
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:53.568
A tool.

34
00:00:53.952 --> 00:00:54.695
A product.

35
00:00:55.391 --> 00:00:57.481
When someone uses what you built, they

36
00:00:57.539 --> 00:00:58.746
come directly to you.

37
00:00:59.443 --> 00:01:00.291
No middleman.

38
00:01:00.987 --> 00:01:02.845
No algorithm deciding if your work is

39
00:01:02.926 --> 00:01:03.843
worthy today.

40
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.235
You control the experience.

41
00:01:06.618 --> 00:01:07.964
You control the relationship.

42
00:01:08.173 --> 00:01:09.462
You own the asset.

43
00:01:09.973 --> 00:01:12.492
And here's the kicker — what you build can

44
00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:14.118
work for you while you sleep.

45
00:01:14.118 --> 00:01:15.233
Let's get concrete.

46
00:01:15.836 --> 00:01:17.322
You're a fitness creator with fifty

47
00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.959
thousand Instagram followers.

48
00:01:19.203 --> 00:01:19.911
Impressive.

49
00:01:20.353 --> 00:01:22.257
But Instagram changes the algorithm.

50
00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:24.648
Your reach drops eighty percent overnight.

51
00:01:24.973 --> 00:01:26.343
Your income vanishes.

52
00:01:26.784 --> 00:01:28.200
Now imagine you're a builder.

53
00:01:28.526 --> 00:01:29.710
You have a fitness app.

54
00:01:30.093 --> 00:01:31.707
Five thousand paying users.

55
00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.773
Instagram could disappear tomorrow.

56
00:01:34.156 --> 00:01:35.364
Your business keeps running.

57
00:01:35.573 --> 00:01:36.467
That's the difference.

58
00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:37.883
One is fragile.

59
00:01:38.208 --> 00:01:39.845
The other is antifragile.

60
00:01:39.845 --> 00:01:41.157
Here's what most people miss.

61
00:01:41.482 --> 00:01:43.258
Being a builder doesn't mean abandoning

62
00:01:43.316 --> 00:01:44.408
content creation.

63
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:45.789
The smartest move?

64
00:01:46.393 --> 00:01:47.066
Be both.

65
00:01:47.763 --> 00:01:49.446
Use platforms to reach people.

66
00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.826
But drive them to something you own.

67
00:01:52.152 --> 00:01:52.941
Your website.

68
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:54.114
Your email list.

69
00:01:54.265 --> 00:01:54.880
Your app.

70
00:01:55.577 --> 00:01:57.074
Platforms are megaphones.

71
00:01:57.248 --> 00:01:57.852
Use them.

72
00:01:58.456 --> 00:02:00.058
But never make them your foundation.

73
00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:02.229
Build on land you own.

74
00:02:02.229 --> 00:02:04.040
Why does this matter for you right now?

75
00:02:04.319 --> 00:02:06.153
Because you're about to learn to code.

76
00:02:06.966 --> 00:02:09.241
And coding is the ultimate builder skill.

77
00:02:10.193 --> 00:02:11.888
It lets you create things that exist

78
00:02:11.981 --> 00:02:13.665
independent of any platform.

79
00:02:14.176 --> 00:02:15.534
A website that's yours.

80
00:02:16.138 --> 00:02:18.076
A tool that solves a real problem.

81
00:02:18.773 --> 00:02:20.422
An asset that compounds.

82
00:02:20.932 --> 00:02:22.709
You're not learning to code to get a job.

83
00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.263
You're learning to code to own your work.

84
00:02:25.263 --> 00:02:26.679
So here's your exercise.

85
00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.849
List one thing you currently rent — a

86
00:02:29.919 --> 00:02:31.126
platform where you're building an

87
00:02:31.172 --> 00:02:31.730
audience.

88
00:02:32.426 --> 00:02:34.446
Then list one thing you could own instead.

89
00:02:35.143 --> 00:02:36.583
Maybe it's a simple website.

90
00:02:37.186 --> 00:02:38.522
Maybe it's an email list.

91
00:02:39.218 --> 00:02:41.169
Maybe it's a tool you wish existed.

92
00:02:41.981 --> 00:02:43.049
Don't overthink it.

93
00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:44.768
Just write it down.

94
00:02:45.882 --> 00:02:47.566
Next lesson, we're diving into the

95
00:02:47.635 --> 00:02:50.015
Nabulines method — how we're going to turn

96
00:02:50.062 --> 00:02:51.931
you from creator into builder in the

97
00:02:52.024 --> 00:02:53.313
fastest way possible.

98
00:02:54.009 --> 00:02:54.892
See you there.
